# Copy this file next to TemucraftLauncher.exe as launcher.env and fill it in.
# launcher.env is git-ignored: the server address never goes into the repository or the exe.

# The folder Apache serves for the launcher (manifest.json is read from there), over https
SERVER_URL=https://files.example.com/wow-files/

# A self-signed certificate: its SHA-256 fingerprint, so the launcher trusts exactly that certificate
# (on the server: openssl x509 -in <cert.pem> -noout -fingerprint -sha256). Leave it out for a normal certificate.
# CERT_SHA256=AA:BB:...:FF

# Only for testing on your own network: allows http, which sends the password unencrypted
# ALLOW_HTTP=1

# What the launcher sends about the player's PC, so you know who is connecting. The login window shows all of it
# (and your note) before anything is sent; logging in is agreeing to it.
# Always sent unless COLLECT=none: launcherVersion, os (version and build), installId (a random ID for the install).
# Add any of: computerName, osUser, mac, localIp, timezone, language, hardware (or "all").
# Every server also sees the public IP address and records whether it let the player in. Log it all on the server
# with server/apache-launcher-clients.conf.example; server/clients-csv.py makes the log readable.
# SERVER_NAME=My Server        (the login window says "Enabled in My Server")
# COLLECT=osUser,mac
# COLLECT_NOTE=Why you collect it, in your own words (\n starts a new line).
